  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A block of metal weighing <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> is resting on a frictionless plane (as shown in figure). It is struck by a jet releasing water at a rate of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and at a speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. Then, the initial acceleration of the block, in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>, will be</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/ad830db4-a562-48b5-8b75-7cc7f177f37b-image.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 87px;\" /></p>",
